{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "ArcCivs 0.1.31: active population and hunger",
  "assumptions": [
    "Low/base/high: 1/10/16 independent cities; one active worker for 1/2/4 hours daily. This is scenario arithmetic, not measured ArcCivs activity.",
    "Recurring auto immigration fills up to 5 living residents. Above 5: one birth per city minute at most, each housed pair needs 20 active minutes, adulthood after 40 active minutes. No offline catchup.",
    "Total population limit stays 12; town hall level caps change 4/8/12 to 5/8/12. Housing changes 2/4/6 to 3/4/6; basic hall beds 4 to 5.",
    "Working adult loses 1 food per active minute. Bread restores 6 food at <=14. Steady upper rate is 10 bread per working hour; initial 20 food postpones the first meal. Hungry <=6 doubles work duration, with unchanged output per action.",
    "No direct Vault/tokens/player XP changes. Native item outputs may still reach existing SELL; future contract-only economy is not assumed active.",
    "Summoning saves travel time only, preserving job duration and paid inputs. Tools and materials move from existing inventories; no ordinary free issuance.",
    "Disposable bread savings are unknown; set to zero, so no accumulation time is claimed.",
    "Owner requested a faster farmer: base native farm action 3000ms -> 1500ms. The theoretical action ceiling doubles 1200 -> 2400 per working hour; crop growth, movement, receipts and finite soil still constrain actual harvest. Hungry new farmer takes3000ms, and outputs per native block do not change."
  ],
